{"t": 46.367, "n": 27, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Rows 3.1 to 3.5 were already built and marked ✓ 2026-11-25 in the plan. The earlier attempt was rejected only because the tests carried the criterion in lower case (`ecc_ac18`) and the proof check looks for the literal `ECC-AC18`. I added a `# ECC-AC18 (ECC-B23)` comment to each of the three AC18 tests in `test_claude_executor.py`. `tests/test_claude_executor.py` then ran with no failures.\n\nI did not re-run the new tests against the old code, so I did not watch them fail first.\n\nSpec check: ECC-B19 in `executor-claude-code.spec.md` still says the private config lists \"only servers both declared and defined\" and is silent on the no-scratch-folder case. The launch is now refused (ECC-B23), so that statement is false. The plan has no row for editing it, so I left it unedited. It needs reconciling later.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran tests/test_claude_executor.py (ran clean, no failures). Rows 3.1-3.5 were already built and marked; this visit only added literal \"ECC-AC18 (ECC-B23)\" comments to the three test_ecc_ac18_* tests so the proof check finds them. No deviation from the plan. I did not run the new tests against the old code to see them fail first. Spec check: ECC-B19 in executor-claude-code.spec.md still says the private config lists only servers both declared and defined, and is silent when there is no scratch folder. The change makes that false, because the launch is now refused (ECC-B23). No row edits it, so I left it; it needs reconciling later.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "68d4f588-5843-462f-b4db-1b626a843b99"}
